      "pot": {
        "content": "```python\ndef solution():\n    # Define variables name and value\n    asset_returns = [2.5, -1.2, 3.8, 1.7, 4.0]\n    market_returns = [1.8, -0.5, 2.1, 1.3, 3.5]\n\n    # Do math calculation to get the answer\n    asset_mean = sum(asset_returns) / len(asset_returns)\n    market_mean = sum(market_returns) / len(market_returns)\n\n    covariance = sum(\n        (asset - asset_mean) * (market - market_mean)\n        for asset, market in zip(asset_returns, market_returns)\n    )\n\n    market_variance = sum(\n        (market - market_mean) ** 2\n        for market in market_returns\n    )\n\n    beta = covariance / market_variance\n\n    # Return answer rounded to two decimal places\n    return round(beta, 2)\n```",
